it's the first time in six years that  officials at this level  have met libya's internationally  recognized government in tripoli  the visit of the egyptian delegation to  tripoli was carried out by prior  coordination between the foreign  ministries of the two countries  the delegation was responsive and  positive in the talks  based on today's meeting we will witness  the development and the diplomatic ties  with cairo  the relationship between cairo and the  government of national accord  was cut in 2014 and around that time  president abdul fattah sisi of egypt  began supporting  war lord khalifa hafter who held  dominance in the east  in april 2019 with egyptian support  hafter began a military offensive on  tripoli  the gna asked turkey for help and with  ankara's support  gna forces successfully retook western  libya  in june but not before residential areas  a field hospital and an immigrant  detention center  were shelled the attacks drew  accusations of war crimes  the visit by the egyptian delegation  comes only a day after a visit by the  turkish defense minister  and senior military officials ankara has  military experts on the ground  and are training gna forces  it seems there's a political settlement  and this visit by the turkish defense  minister yesterday was not a coincidence  libya is increasingly becoming important  regionally and internationally  egypt may now feel that they've lost a  major partner in tripoli  or it may be that they now support a  political settlement  some believe the visit by the egyptian  delegation is a step in the right  direction  we need to ensure that the international  community  remains united but also that key players  like  egypt and turkey are conveying messages  to the parties that they sponsor to tell  them  compromise inclusivity reconciliation  among libyans  rather than launching new and separate  initiatives  the united nations is also working to  build trust between  western and eastern libya the rival  sides agreed to hold  elections next year but they have so far  failed to reach an agreement on the  shape of any new government  although there is some anger over the  visit by the egyptian delegation  many here believe the normalization of  ties between tripoli  and cairo may help fuel a political  settlement to the years-long conflicts  malak trainer al jazeera tripoli
 

